{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8","type":"group","x":-400,"y":-380,"width":2260,"height":520,"color":"6","label":"Six Architectural Patterns"},
		{"id":"c3d4e5f678901234","type":"group","x":-400,"y":200,"width":2260,"height":340,"color":"1","label":"Six-Stage SDLC Coverage Gap"},
		{"id":"b2345abcdef78901","type":"group","x":-400,"y":1640,"width":2260,"height":300,"color":"6","label":"Research Recommendations"},
		{"id":"e12345a6b7c8d9e0","type":"group","x":-400,"y":600,"width":1100,"height":540,"color":"4","label":"Optimization Approaches"},
		{"id":"f8d9e01234567890","type":"group","x":760,"y":600,"width":1100,"height":540,"color":"5","label":"Key Metaprompting Insights"},
		{"id":"e3456789012345ef","type":"group","x":-400,"y":1200,"width":1100,"height":380,"color":"3","label":"Evaluation Methodologies"},
		{"id":"d89012345abcd345","type":"group","x":760,"y":1200,"width":1100,"height":380,"color":"2","label":"Cross-Model Portability & Discussion Stage"},
		{"id":"a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7","type":"text","text":"# AI Harness Landscape\n\nMetaprompting frameworks for coding agents across the six-stage SDLC pipeline.\n\n*21+ frameworks · 6 architectural patterns · 5 harness philosophies · 18 slop types · 212 sources*","x":480,"y":-600,"width":500,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9","type":"text","text":"## Pattern A: Role-Based Assembly Line\n\n**MetaGPT** (ICLR 2024)\nPub-sub message pool, structured docs\n\n**ChatDev** (ACL 2024)\nChat chain, communicative dehallucination (67% hallucination reduction)","x":-380,"y":-330,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"d4e5f6789012345a","type":"text","text":"## 1. Requirements Generation\n\n**Covered by:** GSD, MetaGPT\n**Gap:** Most frameworks skip this\n**Benchmarks:** ZERO","x":-380,"y":250,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"e5f6789012345a6b","type":"text","text":"## 2. Roadmap Generation\n\n**Covered by:** GSD, MetaGPT\n**Gap:** Absent in single-agent tools\n**Benchmarks:** ZERO","x":-20,"y":250,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"f6789012345a6b7c","type":"text","text":"## 3. Human-AI Discussion\n\n**Covered by:** GSD, HULA, Aider\n**Gap:** Severely under-implemented\n**Benchmarks:** ZERO","x":340,"y":250,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"a789012345a6b7c8","type":"text","text":"## 4. Phase Planning\n\n**Covered by:** GSD, OpenDev, Kilo Code\n**Gap:** Partially covered\n**Benchmarks:** FeatureBench (11% SOTA)","x":700,"y":250,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0","type":"text","text":"## Pattern B: Context-Window Phase Isolation\n\n**GSD**\nOnly framework covering all 6 SDLC stages. File-based artifacts in `.planning/`\n\n**Anthropic Harness**\nInitializer + iterative Coding Agent. JSON over markdown","x":-20,"y":-330,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1","type":"text","text":"## Pattern C: Agent-Computer Interface\n\n**SWE-agent** (NeurIPS 2024)\nLLM-optimized commands constraining action space\n\n**AutoCodeRover**\nAST-based search over raw text for semantic navigation","x":340,"y":-330,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"f2345a6b7c8d9e01","type":"text","text":"## DSPy (Strongest Evidence)\n\nProgrammatic prompt optimization\n- ReAct: 24% → 51%\n- RAG: 53% → 61%\n- Classification: 66% → 87%\n\n**Optimizers:** MIPROv2, SIMBA (35%→60%), GEPA","x":-380,"y":650,"width":340,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a345a6b7c8d9e012","type":"text","text":"## Agent Behavioral Contracts\n\n88-100% hard constraint compliance across 1,980 sessions and 7 models\n\nDrift bounded below 0.27\nReliability index >0.90\nSub-10ms overhead\n\nOrnstein-Uhlenbeck drift model","x":-20,"y":650,"width":340,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b45a6b7c8d9e0123","type":"text","text":"## TextGrad\n\nTextual gradients for optimization\n20% gains on LeetCode-Hard\nPublished in Nature\n\n⚠ Gradient metaphor disputed (arXiv:2512.13598)\nMechanism may work despite flawed analogy","x":340,"y":650,"width":340,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a9e012345678901a","type":"text","text":"## Fresh Eyes Principle\n\nIsolating each sub-task's context outperforms accumulated-context by **17.1%**\n\nConductor-Expert architecture:\nSingle LLM decomposes → delegates to fresh expert copies → integrates & verifies","x":780,"y":650,"width":340,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b89012345a6b7c8d","type":"text","text":"## 5. Phase Execution\n\n**Covered by:** All 13 frameworks\n**Gap:** Well-covered\n**Benchmarks:** SWE-bench (~75%), SWE-bench Pro (<25%)","x":1060,"y":250,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b0123456789012ab","type":"text","text":"## Orchestrator-Workers\n\nAnthropic: Opus 4 lead + Sonnet 4 subagents\n**90.2% improvement** over single-agent Opus 4\n\nKey: explicit task boundaries, output format specs, tool/source guidance per subagent","x":1140,"y":650,"width":340,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"c9012345a6b7c8d9","type":"text","text":"## 6. Phase Verification\n\n**Covered by:** GSD, Anthropic, Aider\n**Gap:** Mostly afterthought\n**Benchmarks:** SWT-Bench (partial)","x":1420,"y":250,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"c5a6b7c8d9e01234","type":"text","text":"## Self-Refine\n\nIterative FEEDBACK → REFINE loop\n5-40% improvements across 7 tasks\n\n⚠ Models fail to identify own failings in open-ended settings\nBest for well-defined stages (execution, verification)","x":-380,"y":880,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"d6b7c8d9e0123456","type":"text","text":"## OPRO\n\nLLMs as optimizers generating candidate prompts\nUp to 50% improvement on Big-Bench Hard\n\n⚠ Limited effectiveness with small-scale LLMs","x":-20,"y":880,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"e7c8d9e012345678","type":"text","text":"## LLM Cascade / Routing\n\n~60% cost reduction by routing simpler queries to cheaper models\n\nCritical for multi-stage harnesses where each stage has different complexity requirements","x":340,"y":880,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c1234567890123bc","type":"text","text":"## Communication Patterns\n\n**Structured docs** (MetaGPT): Best for inter-stage handoffs\n**Dialogue** (ChatDev): Best within-stage (67% dehallucination)\n**Spec-driven** (Spec Kit): Best for human-facing discussion (82% approval)\n\nJSON > Markdown for critical state","x":780,"y":880,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"d234567890123cde","type":"text","text":"## State Management Consensus\n\n**Typed schemas** at every stage boundary\nReplace natural language with machine-checkable contracts\n\nHybrid approach: static DAG for predictable stages + agent-driven branching where adaptive planning needed","x":1140,"y":880,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f456789012345f01","type":"text","text":"## Three-Tier Graders (Anthropic)\n\n1. **Code-based** — deterministic\n2. **Model-based** — LLM rubrics\n3. **Human** — transcript review","x":-380,"y":1250,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a56789012345a012","type":"text","text":"## Agent-as-a-Judge (ICML 2025)\n\n~90% agreement with humans\n97% lower cost than human evaluation\n\n⚠ Planning modules in judge were counterproductive due to error propagation","x":-20,"y":1250,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b6789012345ab123","type":"text","text":"## Trajectory-Based Eval (Google Cloud)\n\ntrajectory_exact_match\ntrajectory_precision\n\nDetects \"silent failures\" where correct outputs mask incorrect processes","x":340,"y":1250,"width":340,"height":160,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"c789012345abc234","type":"text","text":"### Critical Gaps: No benchmarks for requirements generation quality · roadmap/plan generation · human-AI discussion quality · cross-stage coherence · harness-level evaluation independent of model","x":-380,"y":1440,"width":1060,"height":100,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"e9012345abcde456","type":"text","text":"## Prompt Portability Does Not Exist\n\nGPT-5 optimized: 99.39% → Llama-3.1-70B: **68.70%** (31pp drop)\nPromptBridge: 27.39% improvement but field is early\n\nChanging models requires re-evaluation and re-tuning","x":780,"y":1250,"width":520,"height":140,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"f012345abcdef567","type":"text","text":"## Human-AI Discussion Patterns\n\n**HULA** (Atlassian): 82% plan approval, 25% PR rate, 59% merge rate\n**Spec Kit** (GitHub): `/specify` → `/plan` → `/tasks` with human gates\n**ChatDev**: Communicative dehallucination (67% reduction)","x":1320,"y":1250,"width":520,"height":140,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"a12345abcdef6789","type":"text","text":"### Agent-Agnostic Patterns\nPlan-execute-verify · File-based state (MD/JSON + Git) · Role-restricted agents · AST-based code search · Context window phase isolation · Typed schemas at boundaries · Bounded retries\n\n### Model-Specific Patterns\nExtended thinking/CoT · Tool-use API quality · Context window size · JSON vs markdown resistance · Subagent delegation mechanisms","x":780,"y":1420,"width":1060,"height":120,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c345abcdef890123","type":"text","text":"## Immediate\n\n1. Build stage-specific benchmarks for requirements, roadmap, discussion\n2. Apply DSPy optimization to multi-stage harnesses\n3. Implement ABC contracts across pipeline stages\n4. Structured artifacts for inter-stage, dialogue for within-stage","x":-380,"y":1690,"width":520,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"d456abcdef901234","type":"text","text":"## Medium-Term\n\n5. Study cross-stage optimization composition\n6. Develop cross-model harness portability\n7. Formalize the human-AI discussion stage (HULA vs Spec Kit vs ChatDev)","x":160,"y":1690,"width":520,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"e567abcdef012345","type":"text","text":"## Long-Term\n\n8. Harness-level evaluation independent of model\n9. Long-term codebase impact / technical debt\n10. Interaction between contract enforcement and prompt optimization","x":700,"y":1690,"width":520,"height":220,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"f678abcdef123456","type":"text","text":"## Key Open Questions\n\n- Cross-stage optimization composition is unmeasured\n- Planning modules: counterproductive in eval but essential in execution?\n- Cost-effectiveness of multi-agent vs single-agent unquantified\n- Self-refinement applicability to open-ended stages uncertain\n- TextGrad mechanism unclear despite empirical results","x":1240,"y":1690,"width":600,"height":220,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2","type":"text","text":"## Pattern D: Orchestrator-Specialist\n\n**Deep Agent Architecture**\nOrchestrator (no code) + Explorer (read-only) + Coder\n\n**OpenDev**\n5 model roles, 6-phase ReAct loop","x":700,"y":-330,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a1b2c3d4e5f67890","type":"text","text":"## Pattern E: Event-Stream\n\n**OpenHands**\nDeterministic replay, event-sourced state, hierarchical multi-agent delegation\n\nMCP integration via SDK V1","x":1060,"y":-330,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b2c3d4e5f6789012","type":"text","text":"## Pattern F: Dual-Agent Planning\n\n**Windsurf Cascade**\nBackground planning agent + short-term action model\n\n**Cursor**\nSimilar dual-agent approach for IDE-embedded workflows","x":1420,"y":-330,"width":340,"height":220,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"d012345a6b7c8d9e","type":"text","text":"### SWE-bench Inflation Warning\n\n32.67% of successes from solution leakage · 31.08% from weak test suites · Actual capability substantially lower than leaderboard","x":340,"y":420,"width":740,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"phe_group_01","type":"group","x":-400,"y":2020,"width":2260,"height":580,"color":"4","label":"Practical Harness Ecosystem (Follow-up 2)"},
		{"id":"phe_sdd_group","type":"group","x":-400,"y":2680,"width":2260,"height":340,"color":"2","label":"Spec-Driven Development Frameworks"},
		{"id":"phe_levers_group","type":"group","x":-400,"y":3100,"width":2260,"height":340,"color":"5","label":"Six Configuration Levers (HumanLayer)"},
		{"id":"phe_node_01","type":"text","text":"## GSD (23K stars)\n\n**Philosophy:** Execution-first\nCLI on Pi SDK, direct harness access\n12+ sub-agents, discuss→plan→execute→verify\nMulti-runtime: Claude/OpenCode/Gemini\nStuck loop detection, crash recovery\nMilestone-level autonomy","x":-380,"y":2070,"width":340,"height":240,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"phe_node_02","type":"text","text":"## Superpowers (82K stars)\n\n**Philosophy:** Methodology-first\nSkills-based progressive disclosure\nMandatory TDD (deletes code before tests)\nBrainstorm→Plan→Execute→Review\n85-95% test coverage claimed\n~2hr autonomous sessions","x":-20,"y":2070,"width":340,"height":240,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"phe_node_03","type":"text","text":"## claude-code-harness\n\n**Philosophy:** Guardrail-first\nTS guardrail engine, 5 verb skills\n3 agents: worker/reviewer/scaffolder\nParallel code review sub-agents\nBlocks: destructive writes, secret exposure, force-push\nPlan→Work→Review cycle","x":340,"y":2070,"width":340,"height":240,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"phe_node_04","type":"text","text":"## BMAD Method\n\n**Philosophy:** Role-first\nSpecialized agents: Analyst/PM/Architect/SM\n\"Epic sharding\" into self-contained stories\nHyper-detailed story files with embedded rationale\nTwo-phase: Agentic Planning → Context-Engineered Dev","x":700,"y":2070,"width":340,"height":240,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"phe_node_05","type":"text","text":"## Taskmaster AI\n\n**Philosophy:** Task-first\nPRD→task decomposition with dependencies\nMulti-provider (OpenAI/Anthropic/Gemini)\nMulti-role config (main/research/fallback)\nLong-term context maintenance\n90% error reduction claimed","x":1060,"y":2070,"width":340,"height":240,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"phe_node_06","type":"text","text":"## Emerging Concepts\n\n**HaaS** (Harness as a Service)\nLLM API → Harness API → Agent Query\n\"Open App Store for Agents\"\n\n**Edit Format as Lever**\nCan Boluk: 6.7% → 68.3% from format change alone\n\n**Harness Hierarchy**\nPrompt Eng → Context Eng → Harness Eng","x":1420,"y":2070,"width":440,"height":240,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"phe_node_07","type":"text","text":"## OpenSpec (YC-backed)\n\n`openspec/` folder: specs/ + changes/\nproposal.md → specs/ → design.md → tasks.md\nMarkdown-based, Git-native\nNo API keys, no MCP required\nWorks with 20+ tools","x":-380,"y":2730,"width":340,"height":240,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"phe_node_08","type":"text","text":"## GitHub Spec Kit\n\n`.specify/` dir: spec.md + plan.md + tasks/\n/specify → /plan → tasks pipeline\nAGENT_CONFIG registry (16+ assistants)\nResearch agents gather context\nMartin Fowler coverage","x":-20,"y":2730,"width":340,"height":240,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"phe_node_09","type":"text","text":"## Kiro (Amazon)\n\nFull IDE built on Bedrock + Claude Sonnet\n3-phase: user stories → tech design → tasks\nMCP support, steering rules, hooks\nNot open-source, public preview\nOnly purpose-built SDD IDE","x":340,"y":2730,"width":340,"height":240,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"phe_node_10","type":"text","text":"## Five Harness Philosophies\n\n1. **Spec-First** (OpenSpec, Spec Kit, Kiro): What to build\n2. **Execution-First** (GSD, Superpowers): How to build\n3. **Guardrail-First** (claude-code-harness): Preventing failure\n4. **Role-First** (BMAD): Who does what\n5. **Task-First** (Taskmaster): Staying organized\n\n⚠ No guidance on which suits which project type","x":700,"y":2730,"width":520,"height":240,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"phe_node_11","type":"text","text":"## Anti-Patterns (HumanLayer)\n\n❌ Upfront harness design before real failures\n❌ Dozens of skills/MCP servers \"just in case\"\n❌ Full test suites after every action (4K+ line pollution)\n❌ Micro-optimizing tool access across sub-agents\n\n✅ Start simple, add on failure\n✅ Optimize iteration speed over first-attempt success","x":1240,"y":2730,"width":520,"height":240,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"phe_lever_01","type":"text","text":"## 1. CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md\n\nETH Zurich: human-written +4%\nLLM-generated: HURT performance\nKeep <60 lines, progressive disclosure","x":-380,"y":3150,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"phe_lever_02","type":"text","text":"## 2. MCP Servers\n\nTool descriptions = system prompt\nToo many tools → \"dumb zone\"\nPrefer CLI in training data","x":-20,"y":3150,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"phe_lever_03","type":"text","text":"## 3. Skills\n\nOn-demand SKILL.md loading\nRecursive file structures\n⚠ Malicious skill registries","x":340,"y":3150,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"phe_lever_04","type":"text","text":"## 4. Sub-Agents\n\nContext isolation, cost optimization\nChroma: context rot at length\nUse cheaper models for sub-tasks","x":700,"y":3150,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"phe_lever_05","type":"text","text":"## 5. Hooks\n\nLifecycle event scripts\nSilent on success, errors only\nNotifications, approvals, verification","x":1060,"y":3150,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"phe_lever_06","type":"text","text":"## 6. Back-Pressure\n\nType checks, builds, tests, coverage\n**Context-efficient**: only surface errors\nTerminal Bench: harness > model","x":1420,"y":3150,"width":440,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"phe_lever_key","type":"text","text":"### Key Finding: `coding agent = AI model(s) + harness` — 2026 consensus is that the harness, not the model, is the bottleneck · Terminal Bench 2.0: Opus #33 in Claude Code but #5 in different harness","x":-380,"y":3300,"width":1460,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"slop_title","type":"text","text":"# De-Sloppification\n\nAI slop = structurally plausible but low-quality code that passes CI while cumulatively degrading codebase health.\n\nMerriam-Webster 2025 Word of the Year. Three properties: **superficial competence**, **asymmetric effort**, **mass producibility**.\n\nAI code: 1.7x more issues · 2.74x more security vulns · ~8x I/O performance issues · 20% more churn · ~41% of production code","x":300,"y":3500,"width":700,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"slop_tax_group","type":"group","x":-600,"y":3780,"width":2500,"height":560,"color":"1","label":"Slop Taxonomy — 18 Types by Severity"},
		{"id":"slop_crit","type":"text","text":"## CRITICAL\n\n**Hallucinated Imports**\nPackages/APIs that don't exist\nCommercial: ~5.2%, Open-source: ~21.7%\n\"Slopsquatting\" — attackers register\nhallucinated package names\n\n**Security Vulns That Look Functional**\nUnsanitized SQL, XSS, improper auth\n2.74x more common in AI code\n65-75% of AI functions vulnerable","x":-580,"y":3830,"width":380,"height":280,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"slop_high","type":"text","text":"## HIGH\n\n**Placeholder/Stub Code**\n`pass`, `...`, `NotImplementedError`,\nempty catch blocks\n\n**Duplicate Logic Proliferation**\nReinvents existing helpers due to\ncontext blindness\n\n**Happy-Path Error Handling**\nMissing edge cases, null checks\n\n**Meaningless Tests**\n`assert True`, mock-only tests\n\n**Data Model Mismatches**\nAssumes structures from var names","x":-180,"y":3830,"width":380,"height":280,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"slop_medhigh","type":"text","text":"## MEDIUM-HIGH\n\n**Over-Engineering / Premature Abstraction**\nFactory patterns for single implementations\nNo automated detection tool exists\n\n**Outdated API / Deprecated Usage**\nTraining data includes old patterns\n\n**Architectural Integrity Erosion**\nChanges that pass tests but violate\ndesign intent — \"individually defensible\"\nbut aggregate = architectural rot","x":220,"y":3830,"width":380,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"slop_med","type":"text","text":"## MEDIUM\n\n**Boilerplate Inflation**\n200-line CRUD when 30 suffice\n\n**Silent Scope Expansion**\nBug fix → reorganize all imports\nSpotify: most common LLM-Judge veto\n\n**Cross-Language Contamination**\nJava idioms in Python code\n\n**God Functions** · **Dead Code**\n**Lint Suppression** (`# noqa`)","x":620,"y":3830,"width":380,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"slop_low","type":"text","text":"## LOW-MEDIUM\n\n**Redundant/Verbose Comments**\n`// This function adds two numbers`\nNo detection tool exists\n\n**Naming/Convention Drift**\n`getUserData` + `fetch_user_info`\n+ `retrieveUserRecord` in same codebase\n\n## Root Cause\n\n**Context blindness**: AI generates\ncode \"regardless of whether the correct\nfunction already exists\"","x":1020,"y":3830,"width":380,"height":280,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"slop_scoring","type":"text","text":"## Scoring Tools\n\n**AI-SLOP-Detector**\nLDR (logic density): 0.40 weight\nICR (inflation): 0.30 weight\nDDC (dependency check): 0.20 weight\n<30 CLEAN · 30-49 SUSPICIOUS\n50-69 INFLATED · 70+ CRITICAL\n\n**KarpeSlop** — Noise/Lies/Soul axes\n**Desloppify** — Mechanical + LLM review\n\n71% of devs won't merge AI code\nwithout manual review","x":1420,"y":3830,"width":460,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"slop_defense_group","type":"group","x":-600,"y":4420,"width":2500,"height":520,"color":"4","label":"Three-Stage Defense Model"},
		{"id":"slop_prehoc","type":"text","text":"## Stage 1: Pre-Hoc Prevention\n\n**S1 Init**: CLAUDE.md <60 lines\nETH Zurich: LLM-generated files HURT (-3%)\nOnly non-inferable, command-oriented rules\n\n**S2 Principles**: Always/Ask First/Never tiers\n`Prefer smallest viable diff`\n`Don't add abstractions for one-time ops`\nCommands > prose (0.01→1.6x tool usage)\n\n**S3-S4 Spec/Discussion**: Spec-driven dev\n= \"guardrails set up in advance\"\nPlan Mode separation · Non-goals · Exemplar files\n\n**S7 Tasks**: Chained prompts · Narrow scope\nDelegate investigations to subagents","x":-580,"y":4470,"width":520,"height":420,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"slop_adhoc","type":"text","text":"## Stage 2: Ad-Hoc Detection\n\n**\"Success is silent\"** — cardinal rule\n4,000+ lines of passing tests = context poison\n\n**Deterministic back-pressure**\nPostToolUse hooks (Write|Edit → lint)\nStop hooks (exit 2 → re-engage agent)\nSpotify verifiers auto-activate on pom.xml\n\n**LLM-as-Judge** (Spotify Honk)\nVetoes 25% of sessions\nAgent course-corrects ~50%\nTop veto: scope expansion\n\n**TDD enforcement**\nTests before code · Confirm failure first\nSuperpowers: deletes code before tests\n\n**Self-refine** — 30% error reduction\n⚠ Failure modes: reward hacking,\noscillation, mode collapse, context overload","x":-40,"y":4470,"width":520,"height":420,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"slop_posthoc","type":"text","text":"## Stage 3: Post-Hoc Cleanup\n\n**Five-Gate Workflow:**\n\n| Gate | JS/TS | Python | Java |\n|------|-------|--------|------|\n| 1. Lint | ESLint | Ruff | — |\n| 2. Dead code | Knip | Vulture | OpenRewrite |\n| 3. Duplicates | jscpd | jscpd | jscpd |\n| 4. Deps | Knip | pip-audit | dep-check |\n| 5. AI review | SonarQube | SonarQube | SonarQube |\n\n**SonarQube 2026.1** — MCP Server for\nagent-integrated analysis, auto-detects\nAI-generated code since v2025.1\n\n**Meta SCARF** — 100M+ lines deleted\nSymbol-level > file-level (~50% more found)\n\n**Key gap**: No tool detects over-engineering\nor verbose comments","x":500,"y":4470,"width":520,"height":420,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"slop_context","type":"text","text":"## Context Pollution\n\n**Formula**: CP = 1 - S(anchor, current)\nS = cosine similarity\n\n**Thresholds:**\n< 0.10 = aligned\n0.10-0.25 = mild drift\n0.25-0.45 = misaligned\n> 0.45 = high risk → re-anchor\n\n**\"2% early misalignment\n→ 40% failure rate by chain end\"**\n\nMitigation: aggressive `/clear`\nbetween tasks\n\n## Verification Layer Impact\n\nWith verification: **81% quality gain**\nWithout: **59%** (22pp gap)\n2024: first year AI code quality\ndeclined measurably at scale","x":1040,"y":4470,"width":440,"height":420,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"slop_fw_group","type":"group","x":-600,"y":5020,"width":2500,"height":440,"color":"6","label":"Framework Anti-Slop Mapping — None Use the Term \"Slop\""},
		{"id":"slop_fw_gsd","type":"text","text":"## GSD\n**Anti-slop**: Context hygiene\n\nFresh 200K per task\nPlan-checker (max 2 iterations)\nverify-work UAT\nAuto-spawn debug agents on failure\nSize-limited docs\n\n**Type**: Pre-hoc + post-hoc\n**Stages**: S4, S6, S7, S8, S9","x":-580,"y":5070,"width":300,"height":340,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"slop_fw_speckit","type":"text","text":"## Spec Kit\n**Anti-slop**: Constitutional governance\n\n`constitution.md` at S2\n`/analyze` cross-artifact consistency\n`/checklist` = \"unit tests for English\"\n`/clarify` resolves ambiguity\n\n**Type**: Pre-hoc (explicit)\n**Stages**: S2, S3, S4, S7, S9","x":-260,"y":5070,"width":300,"height":340,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"slop_fw_kiro","type":"text","text":"## Kiro\n**Anti-slop**: Event-driven enforcement\n\n`.kiro/steering/` files\n(always/fileMatch/manual modes)\nAgent hooks on file save\nCode-quality-enforcer hook\nEARS-notation requirements\n\n**Type**: Ad-hoc + pre-hoc\n**Stages**: S2, S3, S6, S7, S8","x":60,"y":5070,"width":300,"height":340,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"slop_fw_bmad","type":"text","text":"## BMAD\n**Anti-slop**: Role constraints\n\nDeveloper = \"obedient craftsman\"\nForbidden from architecture innovation\n\"Halt and report\" on conflicts\nCode exclusion zones\nPre-commit quality gate (SM agent)\n\n**Type**: Pre-hoc + post-hoc\n**Stages**: S2-S10 (broadest)","x":380,"y":5070,"width":300,"height":340,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"slop_fw_openspec","type":"text","text":"## OpenSpec\n**Anti-slop**: Spec rigor (implicit)\n\nCompartmentalized changes\nTask checklists prevent scope creep\n\"Review & Align\" iteration phase\n`/opsx:verify` exists but\n⚠ entirely undocumented\n\n**Type**: Pre-hoc (implicit)\n**Stages**: S3, S4, S7","x":700,"y":5070,"width":300,"height":340,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"slop_fw_taskmaster","type":"text","text":"## Taskmaster\n**Anti-slop**: Complexity decomposition\n\n`analyze_project_complexity` (1-10)\nAuto-expand high-complexity tasks\nDependency validation\nTest coverage gap detection\n\n**Type**: Pre-hoc + ad-hoc (mix)\n**Stages**: S3, S7, S8, S9\n\n## Superpowers (contrast)\nMost aggressive: mandatory TDD\nDeletes code written before tests","x":1020,"y":5070,"width":300,"height":340,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"slop_fw_key","type":"text","text":"## Strongest Anti-Slop by Stage\n\n**S2** Spec Kit (constitution)\nKiro (steering) · BMAD (manifest)\n\n**S7** Spec Kit (/analyze)\nGSD (plan-checker) · BMAD (sharding)\n\n**S8** GSD (fresh context)\nKiro (hooks) · BMAD (halt-and-report)\n\n**S9** GSD (verify-work)\nSpec Kit (checklist)\nBMAD (pre-commit gate)\n\n## Unsolved\n❌ Over-engineering detection\n❌ Comment slop detection\n❌ No AI-vs-human tool benchmarks","x":1340,"y":5070,"width":540,"height":340,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"slop_data","type":"text","text":"### Key Data Points: AI code = 1.7x issues · 2.74x security vulns · ~8x I/O perf issues (CodeRabbit, 470 PRs) · ETH Zurich: LLM-generated AGENTS.md = -3% success, +20% cost (5,694 PRs) · Spotify LLM-Judge vetoes 25% of sessions (1,500+ PRs) · Meta SCARF: 100M+ lines deleted · Verification layer: 81% vs 59% quality improvement (22pp gap) · Slopsquatting: ~20% of AI-suggested deps point to nonexistent packages","x":-600,"y":5500,"width":2500,"height":80,"color":"1"},

		{"id":"dsf_group","type":"group","x":-600,"y":5660,"width":2500,"height":540,"color":"3","label":"Desloppify — Post-Hoc Cleanup Harness (v0.9.9, 2.4K stars)"},
		{"id":"dsf_overview","type":"text","text":"## Desloppify\n\nAgent harness for systematic post-hoc\ncodebase quality improvement.\n29 languages (8 full plugin, 21+ generic)\nPython 3.11+ · 5,367 tests · MIT license\n\n**Core loop:**\nscan → plan → next → fix → resolve → repeat\n\nState persists in `.desloppify/`\nacross sessions. Can run for days\nautonomously (v0.8+).\n\n`pip install \"desloppify[full]\"`\n`desloppify update-skill claude`","x":-580,"y":5710,"width":380,"height":340,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"dsf_layers","type":"text","text":"## Two Analysis Layers\n\n**Mechanical (25% of health score)**\nDeterministic, tree-sitter-based:\n- Dead code · Duplication\n- Cyclomatic complexity\n- Dependency cycles\n- Unused imports/deps\n- Unreachable code paths\n\n**Subjective (75% of health score)**\nLLM-powered, Observe→Judge pattern:\n- Naming consistency\n- Abstraction appropriateness\n- Module boundary violations\n- Error handling patterns\n- Convention drift · Cohesion\n\nRebalanced v0.9.5 from 200K LOC learnings","x":-180,"y":5710,"width":380,"height":340,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"dsf_antigaming","type":"text","text":"## Anti-Gaming (6 mechanisms)\n\n1. **Mandatory attestation** on resolve:\n\"I have actually [CHANGE] and am\nnot gaming the score\"\n\n2. **Penalized dismissals** — dismissing\nwithout fixing LOWERS the score\n\n3. **Cross-checked assessments** —\nsubjective vs mechanical validated\n\n4. **Persistent state** — no\n\"clean scan\" gaming\n\n5. **Numeric target redaction** —\npenalty messages hide targets\n\n6. **Judgment exclusion** — can't\nbulk-resolve judgment-required issues\n\n**Score target**: >98 = \"a seasoned\nengineer would respect\"","x":220,"y":5710,"width":380,"height":340,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"dsf_coverage","type":"text","text":"## Slop Coverage: 10/18\n\n**Mechanical (6):**\n✅ Dead code · ✅ Duplicates\n✅ God functions · ✅ Dep cycles\n✅ Unused imports · ✅ Stubs (partial)\n\n**Subjective (4):**\n✅ Over-engineering (partial)\n✅ Naming drift · ✅ Arch erosion\n✅ Error handling patterns\n\n**NOT addressed (8):**\n❌ Verbose comments\n❌ Silent scope expansion\n❌ Cross-language contamination\n❌ Data model mismatches\n❌ Meaningless tests\n❌ Lint suppression\n❌ Deprecated APIs\n❌ Hallucinated packages (registry)","x":620,"y":5710,"width":380,"height":340,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"dsf_limits","type":"text","text":"## Limitations\n\n**Resource intensive**\n1.2M+ tokens, 30+ min per scan\n\n**Churn risk**\nSometimes produces complete rewrites\n\n**State-model coupling**\nRaw issues + derived scoring in single\nmutable doc → non-commutative behavior\n($1K bounty exposed this flaw)\n\n**Itself AI-generated**\nCreator: \"I didn't write any of the\n~91k lines and barely understand it\"\n\n**No pre-hoc capability**\nPurely reactive — cannot prevent slop\n\n**No harness integration**\nStandalone; needs wrapper for GSD","x":1020,"y":5710,"width":380,"height":340,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"dsf_arch","type":"text","text":"## 5-Layer Architecture\n\n```\nL5: app/           CLI entry\nL4: intelligence/  LLM review\nL3: languages/     29 plugins\nL2: engine/        Detectors,\n                   scoring, state\nL1: base/          Config, enums\n```\nEach layer imports only downward.\n\n**Key abstractions:**\n- Finding (issue + tier T1-T4)\n- Detector (`detect_*() → list`)\n- Zone (prod/test/config/vendor)\n- Phase (structural→style→security)\n- LangConfig (static contract)\n- LangRun (mutable per-scan state)\n\nFull plugins: TS · Python · C# · C++\nDart · GDScript · Go · Rust","x":1420,"y":5710,"width":460,"height":340,"color":"2"},

		{"id":"gsd_imp_group","type":"group","x":-600,"y":6280,"width":2500,"height":520,"color":"4","label":"Proposed: GSD De-Sloppification Improvements (13 changes, 4 waves)"},
		{"id":"gsd_imp_prehoc","type":"text","text":"## S1-S2: Pre-Hoc Prevention\n\n**1.1** Auto-detect linting stack\n→ `QUALITY-STACK.md` artifact\n\n**1.2** Generate CLAUDE.md quality rules\nfrom detected stack (template, not LLM)\n\n**2.1** New `ANTI-SLOP.md` constitution\nAlways / Ask First / Never tiers:\n- Always: run linters, reuse existing code\n- Ask First: new deps, new abstractions\n- Never: lint suppression, stubs, tautological comments\n\nLoaded into every executor context","x":-580,"y":6330,"width":380,"height":420,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"gsd_imp_plan","type":"text","text":"## S6-S7: Plan-Level Gates\n\n**6.1** New `gsd-duplication-scanner` agent\nRuns after plan-phase, before execute\nSearches codebase for existing code\nexecutors should reuse\n→ `{N}-REUSE-MAP.md` artifact\n\n**7.1** Plan-checker slop gates:\n- Flag helpers with <3 callers\n- Flag new abstraction layers\n- Require lint/type-check in `<verify>`\n- Block out-of-scope file modifications\n- Require `npm ls <pkg>` for new deps\n\n**7.2** Diff budget in PLAN.md frontmatter\n`max_lines_changed: 200` (default 300)\nExecutor checks `git diff --stat`","x":-180,"y":6330,"width":380,"height":420,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"gsd_imp_exec","type":"text","text":"## S8: Execution Enforcement\n\n**8.1** Auto-installed PostToolUse hook\nRuns linter/formatter from\nQUALITY-STACK.md on every Write|Edit\n(success is silent, errors only)\n\n**8.2** Stop hook: type-check gate\nBlocks completion on type errors\nor unresolved imports (exit code 2)\n\n**8.3** Anti-slop XML injection\n~200 tokens prepended to every\nexecutor dispatch:\n```xml\n<anti_slop>\n  <rule>Search before creating</rule>\n  <rule>No tautological comments</rule>\n  <rule>Verify imports resolve</rule>\n  <reuse_map file=\"REUSE-MAP\" />\n</anti_slop>\n```","x":220,"y":6330,"width":380,"height":420,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"gsd_imp_verify","type":"text","text":"## S9-S10: Verification & Cleanup\n\n**9.1** New `/gsd:slop-check [N]`\nSpawns `gsd-slop-auditor` agent:\n- Deterministic: Knip/Vulture + jscpd\n  + lint suppression count + dep audit\n- Heuristic: over-engineering, scope\n  expansion, comment slop, naming drift\n→ `{N}-SLOP-REPORT.md` with score\n\n**9.2** Slop score in verify-work\nIf >50 (INFLATED): warning\nIf >70 (CRITICAL): block completion\n\n**10.1** Slop trend in milestone audit\nAggregate across phases, flag drift\n\n**10.2** New `/gsd:desloppify [N]`\nAuto-generate cleanup plan from\nslop report → execute via quick mode\n\n**Desloppify integration**: use as\nengine for 9.1 heuristics + 10.2 cleanup","x":620,"y":6330,"width":380,"height":420,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"gsd_imp_waves","type":"text","text":"## Implementation Waves\n\n**Wave 1** (highest impact, lowest effort)\n8.1 PostToolUse lint hook\n8.2 Stop hook (type-check)\n8.3 Executor anti-slop injection\n2.1 ANTI-SLOP.md template\n\n**Wave 2** (medium)\n1.1 Quality stack detection\n7.1 Plan-checker slop gates\n6.1 Duplication scanner agent\n\n**Wave 3** (high impact, higher effort)\n9.1 `/gsd:slop-check` command\n10.2 `/gsd:desloppify` command\n10.1 Slop trend in milestone audit\n\n**Wave 4** (polish)\n1.2 CLAUDE.md quality section\n7.2 Diff budget frontmatter\n9.2 Slop score in verify-work\n\n## Result\n**18/18 slop types addressed**\n(vs 0/18 explicitly today)","x":1020,"y":6330,"width":380,"height":420,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"gsd_imp_dsf","type":"text","text":"## Desloppify × GSD Integration\n\n**Desloppify handles:**\n✅ S9 heuristic checks (subjective layer)\n✅ S10 cleanup loop (scan→next→fix→resolve)\n✅ Anti-gaming scoring with attestation\n✅ Cross-session persistence\n✅ 29 language support\n\n**GSD must still build:**\n❌ S1 quality stack detection\n❌ S2 ANTI-SLOP.md constitution\n❌ S6 duplication scanner (REUSE-MAP)\n❌ S7 plan-checker slop gates\n❌ S8 PostToolUse/Stop hooks\n❌ S8 executor anti-slop injection\n\n**Integration pattern:**\n`desloppify scan` after execute-phase\nScore into `{N}-SLOP-REPORT.md`\n`desloppify next` into GSD quick-mode\nBlock milestone if score < threshold","x":1420,"y":6330,"width":460,"height":420,"color":"1"},

		{"id":"gsd_imp_banner","type":"text","text":"### De-Sloppification Pipeline: S1 (quality stack) → S2 (ANTI-SLOP.md) → S6 (REUSE-MAP) → S7 (plan-checker gates + diff budget) → S8 (hooks + executor injection) → S9 (/gsd:slop-check + desloppify scan) → S10 (/gsd:desloppify cleanup + slop trend) · Pre-hoc prevents 10 types · Ad-hoc catches 6 types · Post-hoc cleans 10 types · Combined: 18/18 types covered","x":-600,"y":6820,"width":2500,"height":80,"color":"4"}
	],
